-- Explicit ordered scan source: along carries path order; the mask spelling of the same cells loses it (ex17). Twin of 031-scan-along.bqn.
-- A path walked out of index order: entity 4, then 2, then 7, then 1. A mask remembers who was visited but not when; along remembers both.
-- pathCells is an ordered index sequence (visit entity 4, then 2, then 7, then 1), registered as a vec binding — compiling along down to a mask is the exact bug this pair of prefixes catches.
-- Omitted, left to the .bqn twin: the fold total in path order (a fold has no along; a vec binding is not a mask scope) and the explicit prefix-inequality witness — it follows from the two pinned vectors.
--! registry ../registries/031-scan-along.reg

--! out 2 5 9 10
scan(+) Weight along pathCells

-- the mask spelling of the same four cells: index order, different prefixes
--! out 1 4 6 10
+\ Weight @ Mask

-- This +/ total ignores order. Only the scan prefixes differ.
--! out 10
+/ Weight @ Mask
